<SiteLayout title="How it works" description="Swoovr’s approach starts with what you want, what you don’t, and who you’re comfortable connecting with." eyebrow="Connection, with intention" heading="Less guesswork. More understanding." intro="Swoovr’s approach starts with what you want, what you don’t, and who you’re comfortable connecting with.">
<section class="steps"><article><span class="step-number">01</span><div><h2>Say what brings you here.</h2><p>Describe the connections you’re open to, from friendship and conversation to dating or a relationship. A meaningful profile is about substance; a public photo is a personal choice in our design.</p></div></article><article><span class="step-number">02</span><div><h2>Make your boundaries count.</h2><p>Our intention filters are designed around both requirements and exclusions. Sharing an interest in a long-term relationship shouldn’t cancel out a boundary around casual connections.</p></div></article><article><span class="step-number">03</span><div><h2>Discover people on your terms.</h2><p>We’re designing a browsable people grid with useful profile context, rather than requiring a one-person swipe deck. Visibility and contact controls should respect the choices of both people.</p><p>Privacy is reciprocal: private browsing must still respect another person’s choice about who can discover them.</p></div></article><article><span class="step-number">04</span><div><h2>Find a reason to meet.</h2><p>A conversation can become a coffee, an activity or a plan together. Optional venue experiences are part of that vision, alongside the freedom to make your own arrangements.</p><a class="text-link" href="/venues/">The venue experience ↗</a></div></article></section><section class="callout"><h2>Trust belongs in the details.</h2><p>Verification, privacy and support have different jobs. We explain them separately so you can understand what each one means.</p><div class="link-row"><a href="/verification/">Our verification approach ↗</a><a href="/safety/">Safety & boundaries ↗</a></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
